# What Docker must not send to the daemon as build context.
#
# Without this the context is the whole 1.6 GB working tree — 745 MB of root
# `node_modules`, another 30 MB per front-end package, the git history and every
# build output. All of it is copied before the first instruction runs, and none
# of it is used: the image installs its own dependencies from the lockfile and
# builds from source.
#
# On the small instance this is meant to deploy to, that difference is minutes
# per build and a good deal of disk.

# Dependencies — reinstalled inside the image from package-lock.json
node_modules
packages/*/node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output — rebuilt inside the image, and stale copies would be shipped
dist
build
packages/*/dist
packages/*/build
coverage
packages/*/coverage
.vite
**/.vite

# Version control and editor state
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea
*.swp

# Local configuration and secrets. `.env.deploy` is generated on the box and
# holds the Keycloak secrets; it must never end up inside an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.deploy.example
infrastructure/keycloak/realm-import.rendered.json
.deploy

# Infrastructure — not part of any application image
terraform
.terraform
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars

# Documentation and project notes
docs
.claude
.kiro
*.md
!README.md

# Test artefacts and logs
*.log
logs
test-results
playwright-report

# macOS
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
